      <p class="_abstract">If you are creating a snapshot of a VM, you must specify only one volume snapshot class. Any disk that has more than one volume snapshot class is excluded from the snapshots list. A warning is displayed if the storage class of the disk has more than one volume snapshot class associated with it.</p>
      <p>You can specify the default volume snapshot class in the OpenShift Container Platform web console.</p>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>From the <strong>Virtualization</strong> focused view, select <strong>Storage</strong>.</li>
